Package: peopleparser
Title: Parse Raw Person Names into Structured Components
Version: 0.2.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jesse", "Lecy", , "jdlecy@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Michael", "Flanigan", role = "aut",
           comment = "Original Name-Parser author"))
Description: Converts raw text names into structured components (salutation,
    first name, middle name, last name, suffix, and status) and infers gender
    using U.S. Census name-frequency data. Proper name ordering is
    disambiguated probabilistically based on how often each token appears in
    the first-name versus last-name position. First names can be linked to
    their formal names, nicknames and spelling variants, and reduced to one
    canonical form, using a variant table observed in Form 990 filings.
